d to the right and the graph of\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x+3 \\mid\n$$\n\nis shifted to the left, even though it seems like it should be the other way around." 13194139535456 17592186045417 false] [17592186082948 1074 "Remember that $y=|x-a|$ is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units right.\n\nThe function $y=|x-3|$ has $a=3.$ Therefore, it is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $3$ units right.\n\n![](images/eb/ebe57ac4935c6ffc84abf20de2959c0f6f543514821ff32900fba65515b55646.png)\n\n**Watch Out!** It's easy to confuse the translations $y=|x-3|$ and $y=|x+3|$. The graph of $y=|x-3|$ is shifted to the right and the graph of $y=|x+3|$ is shifted to the left, even though it seems like it should be the other way around." 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186082949 1071 "Sketch the graph of $y= \\mid x+1 \\mid +2$." 13194139535456 17592186045417 false] [17592186082949 1071 "Sketch the graph of $y=|x+1|+2$." 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186082949 1074 "Remember that\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x-h \\mid +k\n$$\n\nis a translation of the absolute value graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x+1 \\mid +2\n$$\n\nhas $h=-1$ and $k=2$. Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby $1$ unit *left* and $2$ units up.\n\n![](images/e8/e80f640da0a2e6e6c1e14790f66b6a05747f6149dddc8a14fc48932bd5e696eb.png)" 13194139535456 17592186045417 false] [17592186082949 1074 "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x+1|+2$ has $h=-1$ and $k=2.$ Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $1$ unit *left* and $2$ units up.\n\n![](images/e8/e80f640da0a2e6e6c1e14790f66b6a05747f6149dddc8a14fc48932bd5e696eb.png)" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186083080 1071 "What is the center of the hyperbola \