 $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}=1.$" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186087977 1074 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 2).$" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186087978 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186087978 1071 "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{y^{2}}{5} - \\frac{x^{2}}{25} = 1$ intersects the line $y =-x$." 13194139535456 17592186045417 false] [17592186087978 1071 "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}=1$ intersects the line $y=-x.$" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186087978 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-x)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{5{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186102084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186102085 13194139535456 17592186045417 false] [17592186102084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186102086 13194139535456 17592186045417 false] [17592186102084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186102087 13194139535456 17592186045417 false] [17592186102084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186102088 13194139535456 17592186045417 false] [17592186102084 1075 #edb/ref 17592186102089 13194139535456 17592186045417 false] [17592186102084 1075 #ed