ligned}{y}^{′} & =\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{(2{x}^{2}+1)^{8}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}-\\frac{16x}{2{x}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+4)^{1/4}}{2(2{x}^{2}+1)^{2}}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}-\\frac{16x}{2{x}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+4)^{1/4}}{2(2{x}^{2}+1)^{2}}(\\frac{x(2{x}^{2}+1)-16x({x}^{2}+4)}{({x}^{2}+4)(2{x}^{2}+1)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+4)^{1/4}}{2(2{x}^{2}+1)^{2}}(\\frac{-14{x}^{3}-63x}{({x}^{2}+4)(2{x}^{2}+1)}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x(14{x}^{2}+63)}{2(2{x}^{2}+1)^{3}\\sqrt[4]{({x}^{2}+4)^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186506519 1068 #edb/ref 17592186506380 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186506519 1068 #edb/ref 17592186506417 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186506519 1069 "q-328381" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186506519 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186506519 1071 "The center of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+6x+8y=-1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186506519 1072 #uuid "1b9ba30c-75b9-548b-bbd4-b9dfefeaa769" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186506519 1074 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+6x+8y & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+6x\\,-\\,4{y}^{2}+8y & =-1 \\\\ [{x}^{2}+6x]\\,-\\,4[{y}^{2}-2y] & =-1 \\\\ [(x+3)^{2}-9]\\,-\\,4[(y-1)^{2}-1] & =-1 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}-9\\,-\\,4(y-1)^{2}+4 & =-1 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}-4(y-1)^{2} & =-1+9-4 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}-4(y-1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,-3,1\\,).$" 13194139535456 17592186045417 true] [17592186506520 1068 #edb/ref 17592186506415 13194139535456 17592186045417 t